description:
Design a sequence to capture a 3-bit input signal and store it into four separate registers across four clock cycles. The module takes a clock signal and a 3-bit input `sig`, and sequentially assigns this input to registers `in0`, `in1`, `in2`, and `in3` on the rising edges of the clock signal, effectively sampling the input and spreading it over successive clock cycles. This design functions like a simple state machine, with a counter used to track the current register where the input should be stored.
